Brent crude prices plummeted almost 4% today, reaching a three-month low 📉. The Energy Information Administration reported a significant increase in U.S. crude oil inventories, adding to the downward pressure. Traders are now questioning demand forecasts, especially in China and Europe 🌍. This drop mirrors wider worries about a possible recession and its effect on energy use.
